### Answer:
### Idiomatic DuckDB Solution:

```sql
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.SQLException;

class simple {

    public static void main(String... a) throws SQLException {

        var query = "SELECT * FROM duckdb_settings() ORDER BY name";
        try (
                var con = DriverManager
                        .getConnection("jdbc:duckdb:"); #1
                var stmt = con.createStatement();  #2
                var resultSet = stmt.executeQuery(query) #3
        ) {
            while (resultSet.next()) {  #4
                System.out.printf("%s %s%n",
                        resultSet.getString("name"),
                        resultSet.getString("value"));
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Architectural Context:
DuckDB executes this query using its vectorized columnar engine with automatic projection pushdown, multithreading, and zero-copy memory exchange.
